speechtext:
1.	J. Amable Garneau.
2.	By the Honourable the Minister of Trade and Commerce.
3.	An allowance of $275 to cover organization expenses and for viseing of the returns made; checking them and forwarding to Ottawa; verification of enumerators' accounts and the general supervision of the census within the district over which he is appointed as commissioner the following rates are provided:-
1	cent for each name on the "population" schedule;
3	cents for each "agricultural" schedule;
1	cent for each entry on t'he "animal and animal products, not on farm", schedule;
1 cent for each record of blind and deaf
persons;
1 cent for each record of merchandising and service establishments.
4.	Enumerators have not been appointed.

For a return showing: 1. The names and places of publication of all newspapers and magazines carrying the advertisement of the Department of Trade and Commerce signed by the minister, urging the people of Canada to buy Canadian made goods, appearing since the present government took office;
2.	The number of issues of each such newspaper and magazines carrying these advertisements;
3.	Total amount paid to each such newspaper or magazine for this service.
